- op: discuss  # 5acc
  at: '2026-08-29T02:28:52Z'  # 5acc
  by: agent  # 5acc
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5acc
  clock: 4  # 5acc
  nonce: 5acc  # 5acc
  message: "DONE in PR #620 (merged, dev at 4b5478145d).\n\nRE-RUN ON THE MERGED TREE, all three constraints exercised behaviourally:\n  non-TTY   -> not asked, and NO state file written (an unanswered offer must\n               not look like a decision)\n  decline   -> recorded False, examples directory NOT created\n  re-offer  -> None; the ask callable would have raised if reached, so the\n               offer genuinely went quiet rather than being answered again\n  real CLI in this non-interactive session returned normally, no prompt\n\nTHE ITEM'S INSTRUCTION WAS NOT SATISFIABLE AND THE OWNER RULED. Reusing\nADR-0045 ruling 8's store is impossible: record_decision raises for any key\noutside BACKENDS_EXECUTING_ANALYSED_CODE == frozenset({'rust_analyzer'}),\nbecause a non-executing opt-in is \"a preference and belongs in hypergumbo's\nconfiguration file\" -- and that file is the one ADR-0045 says the tool may READ\nand must NOT write. Owner's ruling: a separate UX-state record, kept apart from\nthe trust store, since a UX decline is categorically not a trust grant and that\nrefusal is a security guard that should not be widened to carry a prompt\npreference. Recorded at $XDG_STATE_HOME/hypergumbo/offers.json, a SIBLING of\ntrust.d. Pinned structurally: same state root, never nested inside the store,\nnever inside the portable config directory -- plus a test asserting the trust\nstore STILL REFUSES this key, so a later change to that ruling surfaces here\ninstead of leaving a stale second home behind.\n\nJUDGMENT CALLS INSIDE THE RULING, both reversible:\n  * The TTY gate is on STDIN. cli.py's existing isatty checks are on stderr,\n    but those gate RENDERING; an offer needs an ANSWER, so the stream that must\n    be a terminal is the one the answer arrives on.\n  * ~/hypergumbo is ITSELF a git working tree, so the \"output committed by\n    accident\" hazard ruling 9 names for analysed repositories applies in weaker\n    form to the destination too. The examples directory is dot-prefixed and\n    tool-named (.hypergumbo-examples/), the prompt names the exact path BEFORE\n    asking, and the README says it is safe to delete and suggests\n    .git/info/exclude. Defaults to NO -- only an explicit affirmative writes.\n\nThe offer is called at main()'s dispatch return, AFTER the command's own output,\nso it never interleaves with what the user ran -- and deliberately NOT inside\nthe analysis pipeline, which is reached from many entry points and is the wrong\nplace to read stdin. The call site swallows every exception: being un-asked is\nthe pre-feature behaviour and is never wrong, while a courtesy that turns a\nsuccessful analysis into a traceback is strictly worse than no courtesy.\n\nFull suite 24,689 passed / 0 failed. repo_tier_offer.py 100%, every new CLI line\ncovered."  # 5acc
